a bare no-init raw pointer `var p *T` is not zero-initialized to nil when its stack slot was dirtied -- present(p) reads stale garbage (non-nil). Manifests on the LLVM backends (builder-comp/-comp-comp/-comp-comp-comp) and native aarch64; the bytecode VM and arm32 happen to read nil. The raw-pointer facet the scalar/array zero-init fixes (2d856a0f, 77bdd64c) missed; spec decl.var.zero-init (§9.2). claude-todo MAJOR (raw-pointer zero-init).
